<!--
  AICreditPunch - wake-up trigger task template.

  Registered by checkin.bat as AICreditPunch-Resume. checkin.bat replaces the
  placeholders before handing this file to Register-ScheduledTask -Xml:

    __CHECKIN_VBS__   absolute path of run-hidden.vbs in the project folder
    __CHECKIN_BAT__   absolute path of checkin.bat in the project folder
    __USER__          the current user name (interactive token, no password stored)

  Why XML: New-ScheduledTaskTrigger cannot express an event trigger, and this is
  the only trigger type that fires on resume. Laptops rarely log a plain "logon"
  when they wake up - the session is restored, not created - so the logon task
  never fires and the resume has to be observed from the event log instead.

  Subscription: Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Power event 107, "the system has resumed
  from sleep". It covers classic sleep (S3) and hibernate (S4) resume, and was
  confirmed against this machine's own System log (2026-09-12 .. 2026-09-15).
  Microsoft-Windows-Power-Troubleshooter event 1 is OR-ed in as a fallback: this
  machine never logs it, but other machines do, and a filter that matches nothing
  is harmless. Systems using modern standby (S0ix) may log a different id; check
  "Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{LogName='System'; Id=107,507}" on such a host
  before relying on this task there.

  Why the wscript wrapper: the task runs with an interactive token, so a plain
  "cmd.exe /c checkin.bat" action pops an empty console window on screen at
  every trigger. wscript.exe is a GUI-subsystem host (no console of its own)
  and run-hidden.vbs starts cmd with window style 0, so the whole chain is
  invisible. The vbs waits for the bat and passes its exit code through, which
  keeps "last run time / last result" accurate.

  Do NOT add an <?xml?> declaration back: Register-ScheduledTask -Xml takes a
  string, and a string starting with a declaration is rejected with
  "The task XML is malformed. (1,40) 错误: 无法切换编码" even though the XML
  itself is valid. The declaration is only needed when a file is handed to
  schtasks /create /xml, which this project does not do.

  Keep this file ASCII-only: it is read with [IO.File]::ReadAllText while the
  console code page may be GBK.
-->
<Task version="1.2" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Author>__USER__</Author>
    <Description>AICreditPunch: run the check-in right after the PC resumes from sleep or hibernate. Runs as the logged-on user with an interactive token, so no password is stored. Registered by checkin.bat.</Description>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <EventTrigger>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <Subscription>&lt;QueryList&gt;&lt;Query Id="0" Path="System"&gt;&lt;Select Path="System"&gt;*[System[(Provider[@Name='Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Power'] and EventID=107) or (Provider[@Name='Microsoft-Windows-Power-Troubleshooter'] and EventID=1)]]&lt;/Select&gt;&lt;/Query&gt;&lt;/QueryList&gt;</Subscription>
      <Delay>PT15S</Delay>
    </EventTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>__USER__</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <StartWhenAvailable>false</StartWhenAvailable>
    <RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>false</RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>
    <AllowStartOnDemand>true</AllowStartOnDemand>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <RunOnlyIfIdle>false</RunOnlyIfIdle>
    <WakeToRun>false</WakeToRun>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT10M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>wscript.exe</Command>
      <Arguments>"__CHECKIN_VBS__" "__CHECKIN_BAT__"</Arguments>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
